         }
      },
      "lang": "en",
      "notes": [
         {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "Web::Simple versions before 0.037 for Perl do not escape single quotes in HTML::Tags output.\n\nHTML::Tags and XML::Tags escape a plain string value by replacing only &, \", < and > with entities. A value interpolated into a single-quoted attribute, as in <a href='$value'>, can therefore close the attribute and add new ones, such as an event handler. Double-quoted attributes are not affected.\n\nAn attacker who controls a value that an application interpolates into a single-quoted attribute can inject script into the generated page.",
            "title": "Vulnerability Description"
         }
      ],
